IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nz-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nz-part5-oversight`

-- Tests for nz-part5-oversight.l4 (ss 114 to 127).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.
-- The sitting calendar below is a supplied input (the Act fixes none): the House sits Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday for 8 weeks from Tuesday 3 March 2026
-- (3 March 2026 is a Tuesday: 5 January 2026 is a Monday and 56 days later is Monday 2 March). That is 24 sitting days; the 21st is 16 April 2026 and the 22nd is 21 April 2026.

§ `A supplied sitting calendar (not from the Act)`

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the sitting days in the test calendar` MEANS
    LIST (Date 3 3 2026), (Date 4 3 2026), (Date 5 3 2026)
       , (Date 10 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026), (Date 12 3 2026)
       , (Date 17 3 2026), (Date 18 3 2026), (Date 19 3 2026)
       , (Date 24 3 2026), (Date 25 3 2026), (Date 26 3 2026)
       , (Date 31 3 2026), (Date 1 4 2026), (Date 2 4 2026)
       , (Date 7 4 2026), (Date 8 4 2026), (Date 9 4 2026)
       , (Date 14 4 2026), (Date 15 4 2026), (Date 16 4 2026)
       , (Date 21 4 2026), (Date 22 4 2026), (Date 23 4 2026)

§ `Section 114 -- Secondary legislation must be presented to House of Representatives`

-- src:779 | The relevant Minister must present secondary legislation to the House of Representatives in accordance with the House’s rules and practice.
-- src:780 | However,—
-- src:781 | if a presentation exemption applies to secondary legislation (or a part of secondary legislation) under Schedule 3, this requirement does not apply to that legislation or part; and
-- src:782 | see also section 161A of the Local Government Act 2002, which provides that this requirement does not apply to secondary legislation made by a local authority or a council-controlled organisation unless the empowering legislation (or other legislation) expressly requires presentation to the House of Representatives.
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister must present the secondary legislation to the House` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister must present the secondary legislation to the House` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister must present the secondary legislation to the House` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister must present the secondary legislation to the House` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister must present the secondary legislation to the House` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 115 -- All secondary legislation subject to disallowance, with limited exceptions`

-- src:785 | This subpart applies to secondary legislation other than—
-- src:786 | secondary legislation made by resolution of the House of Representatives; or
-- src:787 | secondary legislation made under the Royal prerogative; or
-- src:788 | a bylaw as defined in section 2 of the Bylaws Act 1910; or
-- src:789 | secondary legislation to which a disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3.
#ASSERT `the disallowance subpart applies to the secondary legislation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the disallowance subpart applies to the secondary legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the disallowance subpart applies to the secondary legislation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the disallowance subpart applies to the secondary legislation` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the disallowance subpart applies to the secondary legislation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 116 -- House of Representatives may disallow secondary legislation by resolution`

-- src:792 | Legislation disallowed by a resolution ceases to have effect on the later of—
-- src:793 | the passing of the resolution; and
-- src:794 | any date stated in the resolution as the date on which the legislation ceases to have effect.
-- The later of the passing of the resolution and any stated date.
#ASSERT `the day legislation disallowed by resolution ceases to have effect` (Date 10 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 10 5 2026
#ASSERT `the day legislation disallowed by resolution ceases to have effect` (Date 10 5 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS Date 1 6 2026
#ASSERT `the day legislation disallowed by resolution ceases to have effect` (Date 10 5 2026) (JUST (Date 1 5 2026)) EQUALS Date 10 5 2026
#ASSERT `the day legislation disallowed by resolution ceases to have effect` (Date 10 5 2026) (JUST (Date 10 5 2026)) EQUALS Date 10 5 2026

§ `Section 117 -- Secondary legislation disallowed if House of Representatives does not dispose of motion to disallow`

-- src:805 | In this section, the deadline is the close of the 21st sitting day after the giving of the notice of motion.
-- Notice given on Monday 2 March (not a sitting day): the 21st sitting day after is 16 April.
#ASSERT `the deadline for a notice of motion to disallow given on` (Date 2 3 2026) `counting the sitting days` `the sitting days in the test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 4 2026)
-- Notice given on a sitting day, Tuesday 3 March: that day is not counted ("after"), so the 21st is the 22nd of the calendar: 21 April.
#ASSERT `the deadline for a notice of motion to disallow given on` (Date 3 3 2026) `counting the sitting days` `the sitting days in the test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 21 4 2026)
-- Fewer than 21 sitting days remain after the notice: the calendar does not reach the deadline.
#ASSERT `the deadline for a notice of motion to disallow given on` (Date 21 4 2026) `counting the sitting days` `the sitting days in the test calendar` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the deadline for a notice of motion to disallow given on` (Date 3 3 2026) `counting the sitting days` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:80 | sitting day means a sitting day of the House of Representatives.
#ASSERT `the nth sitting day after` 1 `counting from` (Date 3 3 2026) `searching` 400 `more days in` `the sitting days in the test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 4 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the nth sitting day after` 3 `counting from` (Date 3 3 2026) `searching` 400 `more days in` `the sitting days in the test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the nth sitting day after` 0 `counting from` (Date 3 3 2026) `searching` 400 `more days in` `the sitting days in the test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 3 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the nth sitting day after` 24 `counting from` (Date 2 3 2026) `searching` 400 `more days in` `the sitting days in the test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 23 4 2026)
#ASSERT `the nth sitting day after` 25 `counting from` (Date 2 3 2026) `searching` 400 `more days in` `the sitting days in the test calendar` EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:796 | Secondary legislation, or a provision of secondary legislation, to which this subpart applies is disallowed if—
-- src:797 | a member of the Committee of the House of Representatives responsible for the review of secondary legislation gives notice of a motion to disallow it; and
-- src:798 | none of the following happens before the deadline:
-- src:799 | the notice is withdrawn:
-- src:800 | the House disposes of the motion:
-- src:801 | Parliament is dissolved or expires.
-- Arguments: notice given by a Committee member; the deadline; day the notice was withdrawn; day the House disposed of the motion; day Parliament was dissolved or expired.
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` FALSE (Date 16 4 2026) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
-- An event on the deadline day is before the close of the deadline: the motion is disposed of, so the legislation is not disallowed.
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) (JUST (Date 16 4 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) (JUST (Date 17 4 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 10 4 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 17 4 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (Date 16 4 2026)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` TRUE (Date 16 4 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (Date 17 4 2026)) EQUALS TRUE

-- src:802 | Legislation disallowed under this section ceases to have effect on the later of—
-- src:803 | the deadline; and
-- src:804 | any date stated in the notice of motion as the date on which the legislation ceases to have effect.
#ASSERT `the day legislation disallowed under section 117 ceases to have effect` (Date 16 4 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 16 4 2026
#ASSERT `the day legislation disallowed under section 117 ceases to have effect` (Date 16 4 2026) (JUST (Date 10 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 16 4 2026
#ASSERT `the day legislation disallowed under section 117 ceases to have effect` (Date 16 4 2026) (JUST (Date 16 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 16 4 2026
#ASSERT `the day legislation disallowed under section 117 ceases to have effect` (Date 16 4 2026) (JUST (Date 1 5 2026)) EQUALS Date 1 5 2026

§ `Section 118 -- Effect of disallowance on legislation`

-- src:807 | If secondary legislation, or a provision of secondary legislation, is disallowed under section 116 or 117, the following applies:
-- src:808 | the disallowance has the same effect as a revocation of the secondary legislation or provision (except as set out in this section):
-- src:809 | any other legislation that was previously amended, repealed, or revoked by the legislation or provision is restored or revived as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed, or revoked:
-- src:810 | the restoration or revival takes effect at the time the disallowed legislation ceases to have effect.
-- src:811 | This section alters the effect of section 32 (which relates to the effect of repeal generally).
#ASSERT `whether legislation previously amended, repealed or revoked by the later legislation is revived` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Revived as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed or revoked: section 118 or 125 alters section 32`
#ASSERT `whether legislation previously amended, repealed or revoked by the later legislation is revived` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Revived as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed or revoked: section 118 or 125 alters section 32`
#ASSERT `whether legislation previously amended, repealed or revoked by the later legislation is revived` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Revived as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed or revoked: section 118 or 125 alters section 32`
#ASSERT `whether legislation previously amended, repealed or revoked by the later legislation is revived` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not revived: section 32(2) applies`
-- src:808 | the disallowance has the same effect as a revocation of the secondary legislation or provision (except as set out in this section):
#ASSERT `the disallowance has the same effect as a revocation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the disallowance has the same effect as a revocation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:810 | the restoration or revival takes effect at the time the disallowed legislation ceases to have effect.
#ASSERT `the day the restoration or revival takes effect` (Date 10 5 2026) EQUALS Date 10 5 2026

§ `Section 119 -- House of Representatives may amend or replace secondary legislation`

-- src:814 | The amendment or replacement takes effect on the later of—
-- src:815 | the 28th day after a copy of the resolution is published; and
-- src:816 | any date stated in the resolution as the date on which it takes effect.
-- Published 1 March 2026: the 28th day after is 29 March.
#ASSERT `the day an amendment or replacement by resolution takes effect` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 29 3 2026
#ASSERT `the day an amendment or replacement by resolution takes effect` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 15 4 2026
#ASSERT `the day an amendment or replacement by resolution takes effect` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 29 3 2026
#ASSERT `the day an amendment or replacement by resolution takes effect` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 29 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 29 3 2026
#ASSERT `the day an amendment or replacement by resolution takes effect` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 30 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 30 3 2026
-- Published 10 February 2026 (February has 28 days that year): the 28th day after is 10 March.
#ASSERT `the day an amendment or replacement by resolution takes effect` (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 10 3 2026
-- src:817 | Secondary legislation that is amended or replaced by resolution of the House of Representatives may be disallowed as if the amendment or replacement were made by the maker of the secondary legislation (despite section 115(a)).
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation may be disallowed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation may be disallowed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the secondary legislation may be disallowed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 120 -- Resolution or motion is secondary legislation`

-- src:819 | A resolution or a motion that (whether itself or as a result of section 117) disallows, amends, or replaces secondary legislation under this subpart is secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements).
#ASSERT `a resolution or a motion is secondary legislation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a resolution or a motion is secondary legislation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:821 | However, sections 116(2) and 117(2) apply even if the copy or notice is not yet published.
#ASSERT `sections 116(2) and 117(2) apply` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sections 116(2) and 117(2) apply` FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 121 -- Definitions used in this subpart`

-- src:825 | deadline means,—
-- src:826 | for legislation that is made on or after 1 January but before the close of 30 June in the same year, the close of 30 June in the next year:
-- src:827 | for legislation that is made on or after 1 July but before the close of 31 December in the same year, the close of 31 December in the next year
#ASSERT `the deadline for confirmation of legislation made on` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 30 6 2027
#ASSERT `the deadline for confirmation of legislation made on` (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS Date 30 6 2027
#ASSERT `the deadline for confirmation of legislation made on` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS Date 30 6 2027
#ASSERT `the deadline for confirmation of legislation made on` (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS Date 31 12 2027
#ASSERT `the deadline for confirmation of legislation made on` (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS Date 31 12 2027
-- src:828 | unconfirmed legislation means legislation that is not confirmed on or before the deadline.
#ASSERT `is unconfirmed legislation` NOTHING (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is unconfirmed legislation` (JUST (Date 1 7 2027)) (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is unconfirmed legislation` (JUST (Date 30 6 2027)) (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is unconfirmed legislation` (JUST (Date 29 6 2027)) (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 122 -- What secondary legislation must be confirmed under this subpart`

-- src:830 | This subpart applies to secondary legislation if it is made under an empowering provision listed in Schedule 4.
-- src:831 | However, if that schedule limits which matters require confirmation under an empowering provision, this subpart applies to the secondary legislation only if it relates to those confirmable matters.
#ASSERT `the confirmation subpart applies to the secondary legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the confirmation subpart applies to the secondary legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the confirmation subpart applies to the secondary legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the confirmation subpart applies to the secondary legislation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the confirmation subpart applies to the secondary legislation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 123 -- Secondary legislation must be confirmed by deadline (or otherwise will be revoked)`

-- src:833 | If secondary legislation to which this subpart applies is not confirmed on or before the deadline, the legislation is revoked on the deadline (if it is still in force).
#ASSERT `the legislation is revoked on the deadline` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the legislation is revoked on the deadline` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the legislation is revoked on the deadline` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the legislation is revoked on the deadline` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 124 -- How to confirm secondary legislation`

-- src:835 | To confirm secondary legislation by a deadline for the purposes of this subpart,—
-- src:836 | an Act must contain a provision to the effect that it confirms the legislation; and
-- src:837 | the provision must commence on or before the deadline.
#ASSERT `the legislation is confirmed by the deadline` TRUE (Date 29 6 2027) (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the legislation is confirmed by the deadline` TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the legislation is confirmed by the deadline` TRUE (Date 1 7 2027) (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the legislation is confirmed by the deadline` FALSE (Date 29 6 2027) (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS FALSE
-- src:838 | The later repeal of the Act or provision does not affect the confirmation (see section 32, which relates to the effect of repeal).
#ASSERT `the later repeal affects the confirmation` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the later repeal affects the confirmation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 125 -- Usual effect of revocation if not confirmed by deadline`

-- src:841 | any duties, levies, or road user charges imposed under the unconfirmed legislation are cancelled and, if paid, must be refunded (except as set out in subsection (2)); and
-- src:845 | Subsection (1)﻿(a) does not apply to any of the following:
-- src:846 | orders made under section 5(1) of the Energy Resources Levy Act 1976; or
-- src:847 | fees or charges to which section 270(4) to (6) of the Land Transport Act 1998 applies; or
-- src:848 | levy rates set by regulations made under section 41(1)﻿(e) of the Waste Minimisation Act 2008.
-- src:849 | However, this section does not apply if the unconfirmed legislation is made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4.
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `a duty, levy or road user charge` `when` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `a duty, levy or road user charge` `when` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Constituents of the printed item (ruling C): each is cancelled unless the legislation is under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4.
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `a duty` `when` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `a levy` `when` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `a road user charge` `when` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `a duty` `when` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `a levy` `when` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `a road user charge` `when` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `an order made under section 5(1) of the Energy Resources Levy Act 1976` `when` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `fees or charges to which section 270(4) to (6) of the Land Transport Act 1998 applies` `when` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `levy rates set by regulations made under section 41(1)(e) of the Waste Minimisation Act 2008` `when` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `levy rates set by regulations made under section 41(1)(e) of the Waste Minimisation Act 2008` `when` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:844 | revocation of the unconfirmed legislation does not otherwise affect its previous operation or anything done or suffered under it.
#ASSERT `the revocation otherwise affects the previous operation of the unconfirmed legislation` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 126 -- Effect on some legislation of not being confirmed by deadline (whether or not earlier revoked)`

-- src:851 | This section applies to unconfirmed legislation made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4 (whether it is revoked before the deadline or on the deadline by section 123).
-- src:852 | The legislation is taken, on and from the deadline, to have been invalid for any previous period for which it purported to be in force.
#ASSERT `the legislation is taken to have been invalid, on and from the deadline, for any previous period it purported to be in force` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the legislation is taken to have been invalid, on and from the deadline, for any previous period it purported to be in force` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 127 -- Confirmable secondary legislation must state this fact`

-- src:854 | The explanatory note of secondary legislation to which this subpart applies must—
-- src:855 | state (or contain statements to the effect) that the legislation must be confirmed by an Act before the deadline and that, if it is not confirmed, it will be revoked on that deadline; and
-- src:856 | state the deadline.
#ASSERT `the explanatory note complies with section 127` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the explanatory note complies with section 127` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the explanatory note complies with section 127` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:857 | However, a failure to include those statements does not affect the validity of the secondary legislation.
#ASSERT `a failure to include the statements affects the validity of the secondary legislation` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a failure to include the statements affects the validity of the secondary legislation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `The remaining rules of ss 116 to 125`

-- src:791 | The House of Representatives may, by resolution, disallow any secondary legislation, or provision of secondary legislation, to which this subpart applies.
#ASSERT `the House of Representatives may disallow the secondary legislation or provision by resolution` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the House of Representatives may disallow the secondary legislation or provision by resolution` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:813 | The House of Representatives may amend or replace any secondary legislation to which this subpart applies by resolution.
#ASSERT `the House of Representatives may amend or replace the secondary legislation by resolution` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the House of Representatives may amend or replace the secondary legislation by resolution` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:820 | For that purpose, the Clerk of the House of Representatives must lodge a copy of the resolution or notice of the motion with the PCO, and the PCO must publish it as if it had been drafted by the PCO, under section 69(3).
#ASSERT `the Clerk of the House of Representatives must lodge a copy of the resolution or notice of the motion with the PCO` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Clerk of the House of Representatives must lodge a copy of the resolution or notice of the motion with the PCO` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish the copy or notice as if it had been drafted by the PCO` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish the copy or notice as if it had been drafted by the PCO` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:840 | If unconfirmed legislation is revoked by section 123, the following applies on and from the deadline:
-- src:843 | the restoration or revival takes effect at the time the unconfirmed legislation is revoked; and
#ASSERT `the day the restoration or revival takes effect on revocation of unconfirmed legislation` (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS (Date 30 6 2027)
-- section 125(1)(b): unconfirmed legislation that is revoked by section 123 revives what it had repealed
-- src:842 | any other legislation that was previously amended, repealed, or revoked by the unconfirmed legislation is restored or revived (as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed, or revoked); and
#ASSERT `whether legislation previously amended, repealed or revoked by the later legislation is revived` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Revived as it was immediately before it was amended, repealed or revoked: section 118 or 125 alters section 32`
